  "worked_solution": "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x{\\int }_{-x}^{x}\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x[y]_{y=-x}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
